The order used to gather new cards from your decks before each day's study, stopping at the daily limit:
· Deck: gathers subdecks top to bottom, each in ascending position; fastest on large collections and favors subdecks listed first;
· Deck, then random notes: same subdeck order, but within each subdeck cards come from randomly picked notes;
· Ascending / descending position: by addition order (due number), oldest-added first or latest-added first;
· Random notes: picks notes at random, then takes all their cards;
· Random cards: fully random.
Official tip: subdecks always sort alphabetically — add a numeric prefix (e.g. 001) to control the order, or use _ to pin to the top and ~ to sink to the bottom.
Example: to always gather new cards from the “Finals crunch” subdeck first, rename it to 001Finals crunch and choose “Deck”.

The order new cards are shown after gathering:
· Card type, then order gathered: groups cards by template number, in gather order within each type. Official use case — with sibling burying off, all cards of a note appear in the same session but not back-to-back (all “Front→Back” before any “Back→Front”);
· Order gathered: shows cards exactly as gathered; same-note cards typically appear consecutively;
· Card type, then random: groups by template, shuffled within each group — spread apart yet still random;
· Random note, then card type: picks notes at random, then shows all their cards in template order;
· Random: fully shuffled.
Example: with “Bury new siblings” off but you don't want front/back cards adjacent, choose “Card type, then order gathered”.
